      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assaria%2C_Kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first post office opened in September 1879, shortly after settlers from Chicago bought land for just $3.50 an acre.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assaria%2C_Kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1910, Assaria was still a stop on the Union Pacific line that linked Salina to McPherson.",
